  era: "c. 300 BCE \u2013 2017 CE \xB7 Section 36 \xB7 Indian Economy Through History \xB7 Across the ages"
  title: Taxation through history
  text: Ancient texts mention bhaga, a share of the produce, as tax; the Mauryas and later states took around a sixth to a quarter. Akbar's zabt and colonial land revenue followed, and the Goods and Services Tax of 2017 unified indirect taxes.
